+## Bulk, route and qualified (Alex, 12 Nov 2026)
+
+- **Bulk** is 300 kWh or more, or a deal value over USD 20,000 (EUR at 1.16 and GBP at 1.34 to USD). Either is enough. When the facts do not settle it, the size is "unknown": ask, never guess. Relay's code holds the rule (`apps/web/lib/relay-front-door.ts`).
+- **Route.** Every lead gets one: a bulk deal; the marketplace (small: single packs; buyers also get a demand alert); Jules (medium: the guided listing or commercial buyer flow); or recycling. Relay stores it with a one-line reason on the lead card and on the listing (`route`, `route_reason`).
+- **A bulk lead's deal opens when Alex's first reply has gone**, from the card's facts (Relay does it; no job). A lead under the line opens none.
+- **Qualified**: every item on the route's checklist (resale or recycling) is answered or marked "they cannot provide it", a person checked each, and a person ticked Qualified. Price and when are asked for in both asks but the tick does not need them; the deal then shows "No price" / "No date". A deal opens on what and how many alone. Test or QC documents older than 12 months are flagged.
 
